{% lede %}
Grad school gave me plenty of excuses to make things for the people around me: a parody ad, a t-shirt for the department bar crawl, and nametags for our lab's office doors.
{% /lede %}

## Laser-on-a-Stick

A joke ad for my Optical Electronics class, written and laid out like a late-night infomercial: a glowing logo, a "range" chart, testimonials from imaginary experts, a price burst and fine print. Getting the joke to land meant getting the ad conventions exactly right.

## MatSE Bar Crawl t-shirt

The shirt for the 3rd annual Materials Science and Engineering bar crawl in 2012, themed Lumberjacks. The illustration carries the joke: an axe labeled "advisor" chops at a tree, and the pint glass holding everyone up is labeled "stipend."

## Office door nametags

Signs for the office doors in Jennifer Lewis's lab, each lettered in its own style.
